<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF directors want flotation - paper.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF directors want flotation - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senior directors of French defence electronics company Thomson-CSF have written to Prime Minister Alain Juppe to ask for a decision to privatise the group through a market flotation instead of a private sale, newspaper Le Monde reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>A source close to the company confirmed to Reuters the executive directors committee sent the letter on Wednesday and that it also launched a petition to gather signatures calling for a flotation.</p>
</text>
